.if \n[.g] .mso www.tmac
.TH SDL_PenAxisEvent 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_PenAxisEvent \- Pressure-sensitive pen pressure / angle event structure (event.paxis.*)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_events.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef struct SDL_PenAxisEvent
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_EventType type;     /**< SDL_EVENT_PEN_AXIS */
.BI "    Uint32 reserved;
.BI "    Uint64 timestamp;       /**< In nanoseconds, populated using SDL_GetTicksNS() */
.BI "    SDL_WindowID windowID;  /**< The window with pen focus, if any */
.BI "    SDL_PenID which;        /**< The pen instance id */
.BI "    SDL_PenInputFlags pen_state;   /**< Complete pen input state at time of event */
.BI "    float x;                /**< X coordinate, relative to window */
.BI "    float y;                /**< Y coordinate, relative to window */
.BI "    SDL_PenAxis axis;       /**< Axis that has changed */
.BI "    float value;            /**< New value of axis */
.BI "    SDL_PenDeviceType device_type; /**< the device type of the pen, if known (added in 3.4.18). */
.BI "} SDL_PenAxisEvent;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
You might get some of these events even if the pen isn\(aqt touching the tablet\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This struct is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

